{
  "_readme": [
    "#288 FROZEN MONEY-TEMPLATE VECTORS — the cross-language contract for the four mandated pot exits (winner-A / winner-B / tie / refund).",
    "GENERATED from the Rust SSOT (crates/low-spend/src/tower_settle.rs template_settle_outputs + template_refund_outputs — the code that builds the real covenant txs) by crates/low-conformance/tests/money_template_vectors.rs.",
    "A DIFF IN THIS FILE IS A MONEY-TEMPLATE CHANGE and requires the adversarial money-code review gate before shipping.",
    "Regenerate deliberately: LOW_REGEN_MONEY_VECTORS=1 cargo test -p low-conformance --test money_template_vectors  — then copy to ~/bsv/bsv-overlay-cloudflare/crates/overlay-discovery/vectors/ and re-run every asserting suite.",
    "Asserted by: (1) this pin (SSOT byte-compare); (2) low-watchtower cosign.rs mandated_outputs; (3) app/src/lib/moneyTemplates.vectors.test.ts (pot.ts settleOutputs + chainAttribution.ts settleTemplates/refundTemplate); (4) overlay-discovery pot/covenant.rs (vendored copy + byte-compare guard in that repo).",
    "Encoding: each exit is null (the SSOT REFUSES the parameterization at lock-build time) or an ordered list of [satoshis, lockingScriptHex]. potSats = stakeA + stakeB. lockBuildable mirrors build_template_bound_lock (templates derivable AND recoveryHeight < locktimeThreshold).",
    "refundWeakBoundary (present only when it differs from refund): what the two CLASSIFIER sites (chainAttribution.ts refundTemplate, overlay covenant.rs refund_template) derive — they refuse only when fee_share > stake, the SSOT refuses at fee_share >= stake. Pinned so the divergence cannot silently widen; the SSOT field is the law for tx builders.",
    "Classifier sites derive settle templates all-or-nothing: they return NO templates when ANY settle exit is unbuildable — equivalently, exactly when this file's tie is null (tie is the weakest settle exit: winner refused implies tie refused)."
  ],
